# KOS firmware allow list - the owner vouches for hardware here.
#
#   pci 8086:1234     one PCI device (vendor:device, hex)
#   kind typec-port   a whole kind of chip (see `kos firmware`): intel-me, amd-psp, bmc-ipmi,
#                     thunderbolt, network, display, nvme, wireless, typec-port,
#                     embedded-controller
#
# Use it after you have replaced a chip's firmware with firmware you trust, offline, with a
# programmer. KOS does not flash anything and cannot verify that firmware is what this file says.
# Allowed chips are still printed at boot (ALLOWED). The same file must be installed on the
# encrypted root as /etc/kos/firmware.allow (mkimage.sh does this).
# Empty = nothing allowed.
